          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Leibniz algebra
            is like a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magma"} product
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
            however is retained as a condition in its form as the
            = succeed "-property" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+law"} product law
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiation"} differentiation
            (also a
            = succeed "-property)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gottfried+Leibniz"} Gottfried Leibniz
            %em Leibniz identity
            which gives Leibniz algebras their modern name (
            %a{:href => "#Loday93"}> Loday 93
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LodayPirashvili93"} Loday-Pirashvili 93
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Blokh65"} Blokh 65
          %p
            Leibniz algebras were motivated in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Cuvier91"} Cuvier 91
            %a{:href => "#LodayPirashvili93"} Loday-Pirashvili 93
            as generalizing the relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+homology"} cyclic homology
            (
            %a{:href => "cyclic+homology#LodayQuillen84"}> Loday-Quillen 84
            ) to one between
            %em Leibniz cohomology
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+homology"} Hochschild homology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
            that compute
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
            in the corresponding Lie algebra, Leibniz cohomology is defined on non-skew symmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebras"} dg-algebras
            where now it is the generalization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
            in form of the
            %em Leibniz rule
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LeibnizRule"} (1)
            which still guarantees the nilpotency of the differential.
          %p
            More recently, Leibniz algebras have been argued to clarify the nature of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+tensor"} embedding tensor
            and the resulting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+hierarchies"} tensor hierarchies
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauged+supergravity"} gauged supergravity
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lavau17"}> Lavau 17
            ).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            (typically a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
          #LeftLeibnizAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (left Leibniz algebra)
            %p
              A
              %em
                left Leibniz
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              (or:
              = succeed ")" do
                %em left Loday algebra
            %ul
              %li
                a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                (hence a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
                and then often required to be
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
            %p equipped with
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magma"} product
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi v
                                %mo ,
                                %mi w
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo ↦
                              %mtd
                                %mi v
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mi w
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        A \otimes A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; A
                        \\\
                        (v,w) &amp;\mapsto&amp; v \cdot w
                        }
            %p such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the product satisfies the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em left Leibniz identity
                #eq:LeibnizRule.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 3
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo +
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        v_1 \cdot (v_ 2 \cdot v_3)
                        \\;=\;
                        (v_1 \cdot v_2) \cdot v_3
                        \\;+\;
                        v_2 \cdot (v_1 \cdot v_3)
                %p
                  for all
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i \in A
            %p
              This says equivalently that the operations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \cdot (-) \colon A \to A
              of left-multiplication by elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in A
              via the given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magma"} product
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
              of the product itself, whence the name (paying tribute to
              = succeed "\u2018s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gottfried+Leibniz"} Gottfried Leibniz
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+rule"} product rule
              of
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiation"} differentiation
          %p
            Analogously there is the concept of
            %em right Leibniz algebras
            in the evident way.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_lie_algebras_in_lodaypirashvili_category Relation to Lie algebras in Loday-Pirashvili category
          %p
            There is a remarkable observation of Loday and Pirashvili that in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loday%E2%80%93Pirashvili+tensor+category"} Loday–Pirashvili tensor category
            of linear maps with (exotic) “infinitesimal tensor product”, the category of internal Lie algebras has the category of, say left, Leibniz
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %h3#corepresentation_representation_crossed_module Corepresentation, representation, crossed module
          %p
            Both a representation and a corepresentation of a right Leibniz
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            involve a
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            and two
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\otimes\mathfrak{g}\to M
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}\otimes M\to M
            with 3 axioms.
          %p For representations:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [m, [x, y]] = [[m, x], y] - [[m, y], x]
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x, [a, y]] = [[x, m], y] - [[x, y], m]
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x, [y, m]] = [[x, y], m] - [[x, m], y]
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y\in\mathfrak{g}
            and for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\in M
          %p For corepresentatons:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [[x, y], m] = [x, [y, m]] - [y, [x, m]]
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [y, [a, x]] = [[y, m], x] - [m, [x, y]]
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [[m, x], y] = [m, [x, y]] - [[y, m], x].
          %p
            If the two “actions” are symmetric, i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x,m] + [m,x] = 0
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\in M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in\mathfrak{g}
            then all the 6 axioms of representation or corepresentation are equivalent. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is underlying a Leibniz algebra then an action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is by definition symmetric, hence all the 6 equivalent conditions hold.
          %p
            A map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t : \mathfrak{g}\to\mathfrak{b}
            together with an action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{b}
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            is a Leibniz crossed module if
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi for
                  %mi all
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝔟
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  t([b,g])= [b,t(g)],\,\,\,t([g,b])=[t(g),b],\,\,\,\, for all\,\,\, b\in\mathfrak{b}, g' \in\mathfrak{g}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi for
                  %mi all
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [g, t(g')] = [g, g'] = [t(g), g'],\,\,\,\, for all\,\,\, g, g' \in\mathfrak{g}
          %h3#abelian_extensions Abelian extensions
          %p
            Abelian extension of right Leibniz algebras is a split short exact sequence of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔥
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to M \to \mathfrak{h}\to \mathfrak{g}\to 0
          %p
            where the mapping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔥
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{h}\to\mathfrak{g}
            is a morphism of Leibniz algebras, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is equipped with induced action of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            with fixed action are defined as usual. This way we obtain a set of equivalence classes
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ext
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext(\mathfrak{g},M)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\oplus \mathfrak{g}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo +
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [(m_1,x_1),(m_2,x_2)] = ([m_1, x_2] + [x_1, m_2] + f(x_1, x_2), [x_1, x_2]),
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x_1,x_2)
            satisfy the following 2-cocycle identity:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [x, f(y, z)] + [f(x, z), y] - [f(x, y), z] =
                  f([x, y], z) - f([x, z], y) - f(x, [y, z])
          %p
            The extension is
            %strong split
            in the category of Leibniz algebras if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a
            %em boundary
            i.e. there exists a
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:\mathfrak{g}\to M
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo −
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f(x, y) = [x, g(y)] + [g(x), y] - g([x, y]), \,\,\,x,y,\in\mathfrak{g}
          %p
            As for the Lie algebras, the group of abelian extensions agrees with the 2-cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi HL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HL^2(\mathfrak{g},M)
          %p
            A
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %strong derivation
            of a right Leibniz algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            with values in its representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is a
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\delta([x,y]) = [\delta(x),y]+[x,\delta(y)]
          %p
            Such derivations form a
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Der
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Der(\mathfrak{g},M)
          %h3#homology_and_cohomology Homology and cohomology
          %p
            The homology and cohomology of Leibniz algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            with abelian
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            in the case of homology and a representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            in the case of cohomology:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi HL
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Tor
                    %mo *
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mi Lie
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HL_*(\mathfrak{g},A) = Tor^{U\mathfrak{g}}_*(U(\mathfrak{g}_{Lie}),A) ,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi HL
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ext
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mi Lie
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HL^*(\mathfrak{g},M) = Ext_{U\mathfrak{g}}^*(U(\mathfrak{g}_{Lie}),A)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mi Lie
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathfrak{g}_{Lie})
            is the universal enveloping of the maximal Lie algebra quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mi Lie
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_{Lie}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\mathfrak{g}
            is the universal enveloping of a Leibniz algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          %p
            Fopr
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\geq 0
            = succeed "-cocycles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^n(\mathfrak{g}, M) = Hom_k(\mathfrak{g}^{\otimes n}, M)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^n : C^n(\mathfrak{g}, M)\to C^{n+1}(\mathfrak{g}, M)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mi n
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo +
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d^n f) (x_1, . . . , x_{n+1}) = [x_1,f(x_2,\ldots,x_{n+1})] +\sum_{n+1}^{i=2} (-1)^i [f(x_1,\ldots, \hat{x}_i, \ldots, x_{n+1}), x_i]
          %p
            Notice a difference from the Lie algebra cocycles where instead of a tensor power we have an external power. Then
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi HL
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi d
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HL^*(\mathfrak{g},M) = H^*(C^*(\mathfrak{g}, M),d^*)
          %p
            There are standard interpretations of cocycles in low dimensions. For example for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi HL
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HL^0(\mathfrak{g}, M)
            is the submodule of invariants. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
            there is a natural projection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Der
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi HL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Der(\mathfrak{g},M)\to HL^1(\mathfrak{g},M)
            whose kernel is generated by inner derivations.
          %h3#relation_to_zinbiel_algebras Relation to Zinbiel algebras
          %p
            The Leibniz operad is quadratic Koszul algebra whose Koszul dual operad is called the operad of dual Leibniz algebras or of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zinbiel+algebra"} Zinbiel algebra
          %h3#LieThirdTheorem Lie’s third theorem for Leibniz algebras
          %p
            In complete analogy to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
            and the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Lie+groups"} local Lie groups
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie%27s+third+theorem"}> Lie's third theorem
            ), the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of Leibniz algebras is equivalent to the category of local pointed augmented Lie
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/racks"} racks
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Covez10"} Covez 10
          %p
            This equivalence restricts to the equivalence between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Lie+groups"} local Lie groups
          %p
            Here a local pointed augmented Lie
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rack"} rack
            is a pointed augmented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rack"} rack
            object in the category of germs of pointed smooth manifolds. An
            %strong augmented rack
            is a triple
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G,X,p\colon X\to G)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-set"} G-set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} map of sets
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(g\cdot x)=g p(x)g^{-1}
            %strong pointed
            if there is an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\in X
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(1)=1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\cdot 1=1
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\in G
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G,X,p)
            is an augmented rack, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            can be made into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rack"} rack
            as follows:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ▹
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\triangleright y = p(x)\cdot y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G,X,p)
            is a pointed augmented rack, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a pointed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rack"} rack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\in X
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ▹
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\triangleright x=x
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ▹
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\triangleright 1=1
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#basic_examples Basic examples
          %ul
            %li
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              is a Leibniz algebra that happens to have skew-symmetric product. Conversely, a Leibniz algebra with skew-symmetric product is a Lie algebra.
          %h3#FromLieModulesAndEmbeddingTensors From Lie modules and embedding tensors
          #LeibnizAlgebraFromLieModuleAndEmbeddingTensor.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leibniz+algebra"} Leibniz algebra
                from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+module"} Lie module
                with
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+tensor"} embedding tensor
            %p Let
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                  be a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi V
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi ρ
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} \otimes V \overset{\rho}{\longrightarrow} V
                  be a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+representation"} Lie algebra representation
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Θ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta \colon V \longrightarrow \mathfrak{g}
                  be an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+tensor"} embedding tensor
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
                  such that the “quadratic constraint” is satisfied: for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1, v_2 \in V
                  we have
                #eq:QuadraticConstraintForEmbeddingTenson.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi Θ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Θ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Θ
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi ρ
                          %mrow
                            %mi Θ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [\Theta(v_1), \Theta(v_2)]
                        \\;=\;
                        \\Theta
                        \\big(
                        \\rho_{\Theta(v_1)}(v_2)
                        \\big)
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leibniz+algebra"} Leibniz algebra
              with product defined by
            #eq:LeibnizProductFromEmbeddingTensor.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mrow
                        %mi Θ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    v_1 \cdot v_2
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\rho_{\Theta(v_1)}(v_2)
            %p
              and with respect to this the
              %em quadratic constraint
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:QuadraticConstraintForEmbeddingTenson"} (2)
              becomes the condition that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leibniz+algebras"} Leibniz algebras
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lavau17"}> Lavau 17, Example 3
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We directly check the Leibniz rule
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LeibnizRule"} (1)
              as follows:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi ρ
                              %mrow
                                %mi Θ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi v
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi ρ
                              %mrow
                                %mi Θ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi v
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi ρ
                              %munder
                                %munder
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                    %mi Θ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %msub
                                      %mi v
                                      %mn 1
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi Θ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %msub
                                      %mi v
                                      %mn 2
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                  %mo ⏟
                                %mrow
                                  %mo =
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ρ
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi Θ
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %msub
                                        %mi v
                                        %mn 1
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi v
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %msub
                              %mi ρ
                              %mrow
                                %mi Θ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi v
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi ρ
                              %mrow
                                %mi Θ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi v
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo +
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    v_1 \cdot (v_2 \cdot v_3)
                    \&amp; =
                    \\rho_{\Theta(v_1)}
                    \\big(
                    \\rho_{\Theta(v_2)}(v_3)
                    \\big)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\rho_{
                    \\underset{
                    \= \rho_{\Theta(v_1)}(v_2)
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    [\Theta(v_1), \Theta(v_2)]
                    }
                    }
                    }(v_3)
                    +
                    \\rho_{\Theta(v_2)}
                    \\big(
                    \\rho_{\Theta(v_1)}(v_3)
                    \\big)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    (v_1 \cdot v_2) \cdot v_3
                    +
                    v_2 \cdot (v_1 \cdot v_3)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              Here the first line is the definition
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LeibnizProductFromEmbeddingTensor"} (3)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+action+property"} Lie action property
              (
              %a{:href => "Lie+algebra+representation#eq:LieActionProperty"}> here
              ), under the brace we use the quadratic constraint
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:QuadraticConstraintForEmbeddingTenson"} (2)
              on the embedding tensor, and in the last line we observe again the definition
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LeibnizProductFromEmbeddingTensor"} (3)
          %h3#LeibnizAlgebrasFromDgLieAlgebras From dg-Lie algebras
          #LeibnizAlgebraFromdgLieAlgebra.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leibniz+algebra"} Leibniz algebra
                from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((V_\bullet, \partial), [-,-])
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
              with underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V_\bullet, \partial)
              and with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+bracket"} super Lie bracket
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]
            %p
              On the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi V
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{V}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\underset{n}{\oplus} V_n
                    \\;\in\;
                    Vect
            %p
              of all the component
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magma"} product
              given by the formula
            #eq:LeibnizProductFromdgLieAlgebra.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi V
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi V
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi v
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mi v
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi w
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mo ≔
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi v
                                %mo ,
                                %mi w
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{V} \otimes \mathbf{V}
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    \\mathbf{V}
                    \\\
                    (v,w)
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    v \cdot w
                    \\mathrlap{
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    [\partial v, w]
                    }
                    }
            %p
              Then: Restricted to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \subset \mathbf{V}
              this product gives a left Leibniz algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V_1, \cdot)
              (Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftLeibnizAlgebra"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LeibnizRule"} (1)
          %p
            This statement is highlighted in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#LavauPalmkvist19"} Lavau-Palmkvist 19, 2.1
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p We directly compute as follows:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                            %mo ∂
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo ∂
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo ∂
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mo ∂
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo +
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mover
                                %mover
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi deg
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %msub
                                      %mi v
                                      %mn 1
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo −
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi deg
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %msub
                                      %mi v
                                      %mn 2
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo −
                                    %mn 2
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo ⏞
                                %mrow
                                  %mo =
                                  %mn 0
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                            %mo ∂
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo ∂
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                            %mo ∂
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mo ∂
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo +
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                            %mo ∂
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo ∂
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo +
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    v_1 \cdot (v_2 \cdot v_3)
                    \&amp; =
                    \\big[
                    \\partial v_1
                    ,
                    [
                    \\partial
                    v_2,
                    v_3
                    ]
                    \\big]
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\big[
                    [
                    \\partial v_1
                    ,
                    \\partial v_2
                    ],
                    v_3
                    \\big]
                    \\;+\;
                    (-1)^{
                    \\overset{= 0}{
                    \\overbrace{
                    (deg(v_1)-1)
                    (deg(v_2)-2)
                    }
                    }
                    }
                    \\big[
                    \\partial v_2,
                    [\partial v_1, v_3]
                    \\big]
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\big[
                    \\partial
                    [
                    v_1
                    ,
                    \\partial v_2
                    ],
                    v_3
                    \\big]
                    \\;+\;
                    \\big[
                    \\partial v_2,
                    [\partial v_1, v_3]
                    \\big]
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    (v_1 \cdot v_2) \cdot v_3
                    \\;+\;
                    v_2 \cdot (v_1 \cdot v_3)
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              Here the first line is the definition
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LeibnizProductFromdgLieAlgebra"} (4)
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "super+Lie+algebra#eq:GradedJacobiIdentity"} graded Jacobi identity
              = succeed "-property" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LeibnizProductFromdgLieAlgebra"} (4)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i \in V_1
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The construction in Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeibnizAlgebraFromdgLieAlgebra"}
              evidently extends to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dgLieAlg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgLieAlg
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebras"} dg-Lie algebras
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi LeibAlg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LeibAlg
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leibniz+algebras"} Leibniz algebras
              (both over the given
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+ring"} ground ring
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            #eq:FunctorFromdgLieAlgebrasToLeibnizAlgebras.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
