          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Named after
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G.+W.+Leibniz"} G. W. Leibniz
          %p
            The idea of
            = succeed "," do
              %em Leibniz algebra
          %ul
            %li#Blokh65
              A. Blokh,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A generalization of the concept of Lie algebra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://mi.mathnet.ru/eng/dan31825"} mathrunet:dan31825
          %p
            The concept was revived (and apparently the name
            %em Leibniz algebra
            was first chosen) in
          %ul
            %li#Loday93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Loday"}> Jean-Louis Loday
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Une version non commutative des algèbres de Lie: les algèbres de Leibniz
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=RCP25_1993__44__127_0"} numdam:RCP25_1993__44__127_0
            %li#LodayPirashvili93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Loday"}> Jean-Louis Loday
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Teimuraz+Pirashvili"} Teimuraz Pirashvili
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Universal enveloping algebras of Leibniz algebras and (co)homology
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 296
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01445099"} doi:10.1007/BF01445099
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www-irma.u-strasbg.fr/~loday/PAPERS/93LodayPira%28Leibniz%29.pdf"} pdf
          %p Early review is in
          %ul
            %li#Cuvier94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Cuvier"}> Christian Cuvier
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algèbres de Leibnitz: définitions, propriétés
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.24033/asens.1687"} doi:10.24033/asens.1687
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leibniz_algebra"} Leibniz algebra
          %p
            Relaization of Leibniz algebras as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+objects"} Lie algebra objects
            in a suitable
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
          %ul
            %li#LodayPirashvili98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Loday"}> Jean-Louis Loday
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Teimuraz+Pirashvili"} Teimuraz Pirashvili
              = succeed "," do
                %em The tensor category of linear maps and Leibniz algebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1023/B:GEOR.0000008125.26487.f3"} doi:10.1023/B:GEOR.0000008125.26487.f3
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+homology"} Hochschild homology
          %ul
            %li#Cuvier91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Cuvier"}> Christian Cuvier
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homologie de Leibniz et homologie de Hochschild
            %li
              %p
                Jerry M. Lodder,
                = succeed "Leibniz" do
                  %em
                    Leibniz homology, characteristic classes and K-theory,
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0493"} K-theory archive/0493
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9808036"} arXiv:math/9808036
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Loday"}> Jean-Louis Loday
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic K-theory and the conjectural Leibniz K-theory
                = succeed ".pdf)" do
                  %a{:href => "https://web.archive.org/web/20111230132653/http://www-irma.u-strasbg.fr/~loday/PAPERS/2003Loday(LeibnizConj"} pdf
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1023/B:KTHE.0000018382.90150.ce"} doi
          %p This is partly based on earlier insights of Kinyon and Weinstein:
          %ul
            %li
              Michael K. Kinyon,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Leibniz algebras, Lie racks, and digroups
              = succeed ":1" do
                %strong 17
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0403509"} arxiv:math.GR/0403509
          %h3#relation_to_dglie_algebras_and_tensor_hierarchies Relation to dg-Lie algebras and tensor hierarchies
          %p
            Relation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leibniz+algebras"} Leibniz algebras
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebras"} dg-Lie algebras
            such as the
